{"actions":[{"date":"2025-06-20","source":"House floor actions","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 131.","type":"Calendars"},{"date":"2025-06-20","source":"House floor actions","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Financial Services. H. Rept. 119-164.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-06-20","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Financial Services. H. Rept. 119-164.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-05-21","source":"House committee actions","text":"Ordered to be Reported (Amended) by the Yeas and Nays: 33 - 19.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-05-21","source":"House committee actions","text":"Committee Consideration and Mark-up Session Held","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-04-08","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Financial Services.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-04-08","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-04-08","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"amendments":{"items":[],"total":0},"analysis_status":"scored","bipartisan_band":null,"chamber":"House","committees":[{"activities":[{"date":"2025-06-20","name":"Reported By"},{"date":"2025-05-21","name":"Markup By"},{"date":"2025-04-08","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsba00","name":"Financial Services Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":19,"fetched_at":"2026-10-25T19:39:27+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-25","importance":null,"viability":47.4},{"day":"2026-10-26","importance":50,"viability":47.4}],"id":"119-hr-2702","importance":50,"importance_band":"moderate","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":52.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"The bill applies to all federal banking agencies, depository institutions, and insured credit unions nationwide.","evidence":"Each Federal banking agency shall remove from any guidance, rule, examination manual, or similar document... any reference to reputational risk","evidence_verified":false,"key":"population","score":70},{"assessment":"Federal banking agencies are barred from using reputational risk in rules, examinations, ratings, or enforcement actions, changing how institutions are supervised.","evidence":"No Federal banking agency may engage in any activity concerning or related to the regulation, supervision, or examination of the reputational risk","evidence_verified":true,"key":"magnitude","score":50},{"assessment":"The source material does not state specific federal spending or revenue changes, requiring only an implementation report within 180 days.","evidence":"Not later than 180 days after the date of enactment of this Act, each Federal banking agency shall submit... a report","evidence_verified":false,"key":"fiscal","score":10},{"assessment":"The bill amends the regulatory practices and supervisory documentation of all federal banking agencies concerning depository institutions.","evidence":"Each Federal banking agency shall remove from any guidance, rule, examination manual, or similar document... any reference to reputational risk","evidence_verified":false,"key":"scope","score":60},{"assessment":"The prohibition on considering reputational risk is permanent and applies nationwide to all federal banking agencies and depository institutions.","evidence":"No Federal banking agency may engage in any activity concerning or related to the regulation, supervision, or examination of the reputational risk","evidence_verified":true,"key":"duration","score":70}],"missing_information":["Specific quantitative fiscal costs or budgetary appropriations for implementing the reporting and removal requirements."],"rationale":"The bill prohibits federal banking agencies from considering reputational risk when regulating or supervising depository institutions and credit unions. It affects all federal banking agencies and depository institutions nationwide by requiring them to rem